SUMMARY:PCA Networking Essentials
LOCATION:Julis Romo Rabinowitz Building - 301
DESCRIPTION:Networking is one of the most effective ways to learn about i
 ndustries\, explore career paths and build relationships. But what is it
 \, and how do you do it? This Peer Career Adviser (PCA) led workshop wil
 l help you approach networking with greater confidence and show you it c
 an become a valuable part of your career development. You'll encounter o
 ther situations during your time at Princeton and afterwards where these
  skills are essential. In this workshop\, you will learn: - Why networki
 ng is important - How to build and maintain relationships - How to start
  a meaningful conversation - How to use Princeton networking tools (e.g.
 \, Career Compass\, TigerNet) This event is co-sponsored by Princeton Un
 iversity Mentoring Program (PUMP). and Princeton University’s Center f
 or Career Development. This program is open to all Princeton University 
 undergraduates regardless of identity. Email careerdev\nRegister: https:
 //princeton.joinhandshake.com/edu/events/2045067\nhttps://careerdevelopm
 ent.princeton.edu/events/pca-networking-essentials
URL:https://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/pca-networking-essenti
 als
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
