SUMMARY:From Blueprint to Built: Inside Construction Management and Desig
 n-Build
LOCATION:Center for Career Development
DESCRIPTION:How does an idea become a building? Join Shawmut Design and C
 onstruction for an inside look at the people\, decisions and collaborati
 on that bring projects to life. This session will introduce Shawmut and 
 explore the roles of a general contractor\, construction manager and des
 ign-builder—from early planning and budgeting through construction and
  turnover. A deeper dive into design-build will explain how this particu
 lar project delivery method brings design and construction together unde
 r one contract\, how it differs from other delivery methods and how this
  integrated approach can support collaboration\, cost control\, and fast
 er project delivery. This event is in collaboration with the Princeton U
 niversity Student Chapter of ASCE.\nRegister: https://princeton.joinhand
 shake.com/edu/events/2060220\nhttps://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/ev
 ents/blueprint-built-inside-construction-management-and-design-build
URL:https://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/blueprint-built-inside
 -construction-management-and-design-build
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
